.\" ln.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX ln(1) utility, which this tree
.\" does not provide. An original page (this project's own text), so
.\" it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code, same
.\" posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec 5
.\" ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-litigated.
.\" Rendered at build time to build/man/LN.TXT and staged on the
.\" play image as /usr/man/LN.
.TH LN 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
ln \- link files
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ln
is not provided on maux.
ProDOS has no hard links, no symbolic links, and no named pipes
(docs/ANACHRONISMS.md sec W2).
